<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richborough</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rutupiae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richborough, Roman Rutupiae, is a site near Sandwich in Kent, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, where the Roman army landed in the invasion of 43 CE. It became a major port and supply base, marked in the late 1st century by a huge monumental arch, and in the 3rd century a fort of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> Shore. Its ruined walls are now in the care of English Heritage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/richborough.jpg" alt="Richborough" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Des Blenkinsopp · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Richborough_Castle_Entrance_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3295740.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
